<title>POLAND: Polish president signs 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Polish president signs 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish President Aleksander Kwasniewski on Monday signed into law the 1997 budget draft, the presidential press office said.</p>
<p>The bill, seen as the continuation of the three previous budgets of the ruling leftist coalition, envisages cutting year-on-year inflation to 13 percent in December 1997 from last year's 18.5 percent.</p>
<p>It provides for keeping GDP growth rate at 5.5 percent and slightly increasing real-term spending for most underfinanced areas such as education, health care, justice system and defence. @</p>
<p>On Friday, the lower house of parliament gave a final go-ahead to the bill after rejecting proposals to boost spending on agriculture put forward by the upper house.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
